## Key Learning

Before planning disruptive recovery procedures such as rescue mode or server reboot, it is important to verify whether an authenticated root session 
already exists on the system console. In this incident, an existing root console session provided the necessary administrative access to restore 
ownership of critical operating system files, avoiding downtime and resolving a month-old issue without impacting production services.
